    "who": "leon",
    "message": "That pattern — pain on the **outside of the knee**, worse later in long runs, gone after rest — is very typical of **IT band syndrome**, but I cannot diagnose it. What usually helps:\n\n- Cut the long run back by 20–30 % for a week or two.\n- Strengthen hips: side planks, clamshells, single‑leg squats, 3× per week.\n- Check your shoes’ mileage; past ~700 km they often contribute.\n\nIf it becomes sharp during short runs, or swells, see a physio — Kiné Sport Croix‑Rousse had good reviews when you asked in July.",
